{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-30fb-71f2-83a8-87f50d0f5179","id":"01a1a587-e7b4-72b2-9d9e-96381afac46e","idempotency_key":"3e8d9cc44e6ad096b4b5a0550bd55eb43e31eef1b1eda26807353c895b0a069f","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T07:48:29Z","payload":{"note":"crates/ai/src/agent.rs (feature provider): AgentLoop runs one turn from the compiled context through provider rounds and tool calls. TurnPlan/TurnContext carry the context JSON and SHA-256 into every stored turn; one system message only (the compiled context), history and the new user message follow; tool results are serialized back to the model. Policy gate per call: Deny -> not offered and refused as denied, RequiresApproval -> approval_required plus ApprovalRequired event without touching the host, Allow -> ToolHost call. TurnLimits max_rounds (default 6) and max_tool_retries (default 2) with agent_rounds_exhausted / agent_tool_retries_exhausted; illegal results are fed back so the model can correct, unknown tools and invalid arguments are results not panics. Cancellation is checked before every provider round and before every tool call, so no write happens after stop. Emits AiEventPayload TurnStarted/ContextReady/ContentDelta/ReasoningDelta/ToolCall/ToolResult/BoardAction/ApprovalRequired/Usage/Error/TurnDone and returns TurnDraft::to_turn for persistence. Evidence: cargo test -p rbc-ai --all-features agent_loop -> 15 tests (context hash, tool round trip, max rounds, denied/approval, illegal-move retry, retry exhaustion, cancellation mid-turn, provider failure, store round trip of usage/context/error). Adoption still open: domain_api send_ai_turn calls api::chat_with_tools; swapping it to AgentLoop + BoardWriteHost/ReadHost is the next step (t-d0bf/t-2883).","target":"t-7e92"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
